tazchroot
=========

Build SliTaz packages from a foreign GNU/Linux host (Debian, Ubuntu, ...).

POSIX shell, mount + chroot. No proot, no systemd, no extra dependencies
beyond what every distro already ships.

Install
-------

    sudo make install

Quick start
-----------

    sudo tazchroot setup        # download and extract SliTaz rootfs
    sudo tazchroot enter        # mount and enter the chroot

Inside the chroot, on first use:

    tazpkg get-install cookutils
    hg clone https://hg.slitaz.org/wok /home/slitaz/wok

Then back on the host:

    sudo tazchroot cook busybox

Layout
------

By default everything lives in ~/.slitaz/ on the host:

    chroot/      SliTaz rootfs
    wok/         package recipes (bind-mounted in chroot)
    packages/    built .tazpkg files
    cache/       build cache
    log/         build logs
    src/         source tarballs

Override via /etc/slitaz/tazchroot.conf, ~/.slitaz/tazchroot.conf, or
./tazchroot.conf (last wins).

Commands
--------

    setup        Download SliTaz rootfs and prepare chroot
    enter        Mount and enter the chroot
    umount       Unmount the chroot
    cook <pkg>   Cook a package inside the chroot
    clean        Clean cache and build logs
    status       Show chroot status

Notes
-----

A chroot is not a security boundary. Do not run untrusted package recipes.
